{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/607234-so-social-werewolves","id":607234,"title":"So...social werewolves?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-29T16:25:27-07:00","id":607234,"title":"So...social werewolves?","content":"A friend is starting a Wild West game soon, and I've decided to play a Ragabash Iron Rider. My only real experience with Werewolf prior is another Wild West game, in which I played a Ragabash Silent Strider, so I'm a bit lost when it comes to gifts, the Curse, etc.<br /> <br /> The character concept is a high-stakes gambler, petty thief and cheat, and all-around rogue. I told my ST to think of Jodie Foster's character from <i>Maverick</i> to give him the general idea of how she's going to be. Beyond that...I started her Rage at 2, and don't plan to raise that higher (to avoid the Curse); her starting gifts are Persuasion, Scent of Running Water, and Control Simple Machine; and I loaded her with merits/flaws (Lightning Calculator, Eidetic Memory, three points of Lucky, Second-class Citizen being a biracial woman, and Derangement: compulsive gambler). Attribute-wise, she's primary social, secondary mental, and tertiary physical; skills-wise, she's pretty much exactly what you'd expect.<br /> <br /> So...the question is, for what gifts and totems should I really be on the lookout to supplement her? And, for what should I be on the lookout when it comes to being the pack's face? I know enough about Werewolf to know interacting with humans regularly can be...problematic, even for social characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:41:39-07:00","id":607260,"title":"","content":"W20 had a wide array of new social trick Gifts for Ragabashes. As for Totem, that's between you and the other players; it's a group thing, so it has to fit everyone's wants and needs. You can try and steer people toward Coyote or some other totem of cunning, but if the pack was made for a purpose, then that should probably dictate the totem to some extent. The ban will potentially affect how you interact with others, however (unless you get Bear, Coyote, or another totem that lacks a ban. Since you've avoided the mechanical affects of the Curse, the main problem for representing your pack among humans will probably involve your pack twigging people out, so prepare for that if someone's character is loaded down with Rage, and maybe meet people with your pack out of sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T19:00:24-07:00","id":607340,"title":"","content":"It's a Revised Totem, not a W20 one, but Goat isn't a bad option. Goat's bonuses are very useful for the character, but offers plenty to other character concepts as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T19:09:27-07:00","id":607345,"title":"","content":"Hawk might be another good totem, as he gives +2 Subterfuge and +1 Manipulation (an Attribute dot!) to each of his children. And he's one Background dot cheaper than Goat. But Hawk's Ban is that his children must tell one lie for every two truths they tell. If your character is like Jodie Foster's character from <i>Maverick </i>(gawds, it's been years since I've seen that movie!), then she won't have any problem with this Ban.<br /> <br /> SHAMELESS PLUG TIME: And yes, feel free to download my Complete Totems List from my siggy if you want to see ALL the Werewolf totems ever published.<br /> <br /> Also, I think I just found a Totem of Cunning that is <i>not </i>a proper one for your character: Tezcatlipoca. Yes, he has good traits for Ragabash/trickster characters, but his Ban is...refusing temptation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tezcatlipoca tests the Garou (as well as other Fera) by offering them illicit powers or pleasures and seeing which ones succumb. The offers are never sincere, though, and those who accept he leads into situations where they will be caught and punished. A Glass Walker pack in Mexico City that follows him have started to call him the \u201cPolice Entrapment God,\u201d and he doesn\u2019t seem to mind. There are also some Bone Gnawer, Shadow Lord and Uktena packs devoted to him.<br /> <b>Individual Traits:</b> The children of Tezcatlipoca are blessed with the ability to seem persuasive and logical, each receiving +1 Manipulation and +1 Subterfuge.<br /> <b>Pack Traits:</b> Tezcatlipoca also allows his packs to know something about the culture of temptation in any time, offering +3 Streetwise and +1 Occult.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Tezcatlipoca\u2019s children must demonstrate that they are not among those who are weak and prone to temptation. They are not permitted to indulge in displays of casual hedonism, such as drunkenness or one-night-stands. </div> </div> </div>No one-night stands? D'oh....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 07-29-2015, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}